```This is a very real and well-known Android / OnePlus issue, and the fact that it only happens on OnePlus devices is the biggest clue. You're not doing something "wrong" in Unity — this is almost always caused by system UI / safe-area / insets behavior on OxygenOS.

Let's break it down clearly.

The root cause (most likely)
Incorrect or dynamic Safe Area / system inset handling on OnePlus

OnePlus (especially 11R / 12R / OxygenOS 13–14) is notorious for:

Reporting incorrect safe area values

Changing safe area after app launch

Applying gesture navigation insets differently

Treating bottom gesture areas as "unsafe" but shifting UI upwards

Unity itself trusts Android's WindowInsets, which OnePlus sometimes reports incorrectly.

Result:

A panel anchored to bottom appears higher, sometimes near the top or mid-screen.

Why it only happens on OnePlus
Device	Behavior
Samsung	Stable safe area
iOS	Very strict safe area rules
Editor	No system UI
OnePlus	❌ Dynamic / incorrect insets

OnePlus aggressively modifies:

Navigation bar height

Gesture bar behavior

Display cutout handling

Full-screen mode at runtime

The most common technical causes (ranked)
1️⃣ Using Safe Area but applying it incorrectly

If you:

Read Screen.safeArea once in Start()

Apply padding once

Never re-apply after resolution/orientation/system-UI changes

👉 On OnePlus, safe area changes AFTER Start()

2️⃣ Bottom-anchored UI + Canvas Scaler mismatch

If your panel:

Is anchored to bottom

Uses Scale With Screen Size

Reference resolution doesn't match device aspect

Match slider ≠ 0.5

OnePlus' tall aspect ratios amplify this error.

3️⃣ Fullscreen + gesture navigation

OnePlus gesture bar:

Takes space at bottom

Sometimes reported as top inset

Causes Unity to offset UI upward

This is especially common when:

Screen.fullScreen = true;


or immersive mode is enabled.

4️⃣ Canvas using Camera render mode

If Canvas is:

Screen Space - Camera

Camera viewport rect is modified

Safe area applied twice

👉 The offset compounds and pushes UI up.```
